dict(page='f2v',image='https://www.voynich.nu/q01/f002v_crd.jpg',observed='One large notched rounded leaf; horizontal rhizome-like base; tall stalk and flaring flower outline.',supports='Aquatic broad-leaf interpretation is plausible.',against='Flower is not a straightforward many-petalled water-lily rendering. Species characters cannot be established at this resolution.',alternatives=['Nymphaea alba','Nymphaea candida','water plant, unresolved','Egyptian bean / lotus (ELV tentative preference)','Convolvulus','mallow-like plant','Villarsia (historical suggestion, nomenclature unresolved)','unidentified / composite'],original='ELV notebook edition pp.2–3, notebook1 images6–8: several aquatic and terrestrial possibilities; eventually leans toward Egyptian bean. This is not a water-lily consensus.',status='Water-lily candidate retained, species unverified',name='Nenufar: conditional broad fit only. CELT glossary includes both Nuphar lutea and Nymphaea alba; not an exact alba/candida anchor.',refs=['notebook','q1','celt']),
dict(page='f2r',image='https://www.voynich.nu/q01/f002r_crd.jpg',observed='Three brush-like heads on branching stems; green divided or clustered leaves; small curled roots.',supports='General knapweed-like heads remain compatible with Centaurea.',against='Fine bract spines and leaf architecture needed for a species decision are unresolved; diffuse knapweed has diagnostic spiny involucral bracts.',alternatives=['Centaurea, species unresolved','Centaurea diffusa','Centaurea biebersteinii (reported name)','Centaurea cyanus comparison in ELV','Cyanus solstitialis considered with reservations','unidentified / composite'],original='ELV notebook edition pp.1–2, notebook1 images4–5: favours Centaurea but leaves species open. Sherwood original site unavailable; Bax’s report of her species alternatives remains secondary.',status='Genus resemblance only; historical-name pairing rejected as an exact anchor',name='Centauria: CELT glossary dedga identifies Centaurium species and possibly Blackstonia perfoliata. This edition does not substantiate a name for the proposed knapweed species.',refs=['notebook','knapweed','celt','sherwood']),
dict(page='f6v',image='https://www.voynich.nu/q01/f006v_crd.jpg',observed='Star-like deeply divided leaves, stalks meeting near leaf centres, several round prickly-looking heads.',supports='Palmately lobed peltate leaves plus prickly fruits agree broadly with Ricinus morphology.',against='Three-lobed capsules, toothed margins and flower clusters are not securely resolved; isolated ball arrangement is stylized.',alternatives=['Ricinus communis','hemp (ELV crossed out)','bur-like plant (ELV earlier idea)','black gum / arctium / bidenus hypnis (Petersen compilation; spelling preserved)','unidentified / composite'],original='ELV notebook edition pp.7–8, notebook1 images27–28: castor favoured after hemp and bur alternatives. Source attribution now verified through the notebook transcription, not the autograph.',status='Stronger visual candidate; not a confirmed species',name='No period name newly admitted. ELV lists Arbor mirabilis, palma Christi, cici and kiki, but her twentieth-century synonym list is not itself a dated medieval attestation. Trinity O.2.48 is a lead, not a verified name passage.',refs=['notebook','castor','q1','trinity']),
dict(page='f9v',image='https://www.voynich.nu/q02/f009v_crd.jpg',observed='Several blue/yellow asymmetrical flowers; broad lower leaves and more dissected leaf-like parts higher up.',supports='Pansy-like flowers and differing leaf/stipule forms support a Viola candidate.',against='Spur, calyx and exact leaf/stipule distinctions are unresolved; colour and stylization do not fix species.',alternatives=['Viola tricolor','Viola, species unresolved','unidentified / composite'],original='ELV notebook edition p.11, notebook1 image43: initially confident wild pansy; April1952 addendum narrows certainty to violet, with tricolor probable.',status='Stronger visual candidate; species remains provisional',name='Uiola: not a clean tricolor anchor. CELT glossary associates this entry with Viola odorata and distinguishes pansy. Pansy synonyms in ELV need dated witnesses before admission.',refs=['notebook','pansy','celt']),
